stion  actually  so um the idea here is that we take  these markers as a kit it's actually a  bunch of antibodies  that we put them all together in  in in a vial so the way we use it right  now we  we very much use this technology to  detect myeloma cells  in 3d cultures and in vivo and the  reason  is that in 3d cultures and in vivo there  are they develop  hypoxic conditions and a lot of these  cells really lose their cd-138  so to go and detect them with the  classic models  it's useless so what we do actually is  we have a vial  that we mix all the antibodies together  and we just take the same amount and add  it to the different myeloma  samples so to to answer your question  directly  i would think of it as a kit  that has a mix of antibodies that will  be  sold as a vial that the researcher would  take  a certain amount per certain amount of  cells that you want to detect myeloma in  and just analyze it directly by flow i i  would even call it  multiple myeloma detection kit  exciting very easy upscale  it seems so well professor kareem azam  thank you so much for your time today  and for your research and we want to  thank our audience too for their  outstanding questions we hope they found  today's  presentation to be informational and  insightful  now today's presentation will be  available for on-demand viewing  and to our audience don't miss out on  the other valuable presentations on our  agenda  you can visit that agenda tab in the  auditorium for a full listing  thank you again for your participation  and until next time  goodbye
 

